Description: In a 3D project take each 3D clip's views out side by side
 The project's packing came from the first 3D clip in the bin, and every clip's
 frames were composed as they are: a top and bottom clip in a side by side
 project rendered as both eyes mixed in each half, and a right-eye-first clip with
 swapped eyes. Now, while the project's packing comes from its clips (Automatic),
 every clip whose frames hold both views gets MLT's stereo3d_unpack as the first
 filter of its timeline producer (in_producer, the edition's MLT +stereo3d7): its
 views side by side, the left eye first, each at its own resolution and shape, which
 MLT fits to the project's frame once, as it fits any clip. A project frame whose
 shape the players read as half views (1920x1080) gets target_views=half. A clip
 already side by side, left eye first, with views of the project's kind is left as
 it is, decoded at its own depth. The project's packing is then side by side, left
 eye first; frame sequences are kept as before; a packing the person chose for the
 project takes the clips' conversion off, as the frames were before.
